    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104229" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τολμ-ηρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, usual prose form for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τολμήεις,</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Antipho
			3.3.1
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			And.
			1.110
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Lys.
			7.19
		</span></i>, etc.; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ-ότατοι</span>”
